but EPM seems to have better outdoor areas for the wedding such as X-lounge and the restaurants. I am an ultimate indecisive person, and there are so many resorts to choose from. I will keep reading your posts and since I don&#039;t have enough posts, I might ask you individually to send me the attachments you posted here, just a heads-up &lt;img src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/wink.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" class=\"inlineimg\" \/&gt; Anyway thank you so much for the helpful info, I really appreciate it!!! Good luck everyone for the planning and the big day!","Attachments":[],"Id":1093521,"PostDate":1269891247,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Hi Ladies!! <br \/> <br \/> I am a newbie and I've been reading this entire thread because I'm still in the process of finding the hotel for my wedding. But I am now leaning towards EPM after reading all your posts. I am also looking at Excellence Riviera Cancun since that is further away from the Cancun and I prefer more intimate relaxed, but EPM seems to have better outdoor areas for the wedding such as X-lounge and the restaurants. I am an ultimate indecisive person, and there are so many resorts to choose from. I will keep reading your posts and since I don't have enough posts, I might ask you individually to send me the attachments you posted here, just a heads-up <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/wink.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" class=\"inlineimg\" \/><\/span> Anyway thank you so much for the helpful info, I really appreciate it!!! Good luck everyone for the planning and the big day!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"lovejones312@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1269563885,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-226792.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"ReeRee","Id":226792,"Name":"ReeRee","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":27268,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"14b26f825c19c05d3c3f22fa7b45ad80","RawContent":"Caroline 0227 thanks so much for posting cake flavors. I am definitely getting cake 10 for those of you who have the cake option pdf. I will ask Yamina if that will come with three layers as the picture shows, but does anyone have any filling suggestions for the layers? Is it better to choose 1 filling or different fillings each layer. I have not had wedding cake in awhile so I don&#039;t know what I want, but I do want fresh fruit (fresh strawberries sounds great). HELP please :)","Attachments":[],"Id":1094849,"PostDate":1269933498,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Caroline 0227 thanks so much for posting cake flavors. I am definitely getting cake 10 for those of you who have the 