> User acw271011 (232000)
Request Time: 0 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"99.224.73.70","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79893,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1453795081,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"8b41d62f4c0184c7f940c5330a93ca3a","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;I&#039;m leaving for my wedding at Secrets Wild Orchid in MoBay in 2 days and have finally finished my bouquet, my FH&#039;s boutonniere and my grandmothers corsage. I would have loved to have real flowers but I wanted peonies in different shades of coral for my bouquet and as many of you know the prices are crazy expensive (quotes I received were in the $600 range just for my bouquet!) to me that is just too expensive for flowers I can&#039;t bring home through customs to have as a keepsake so I ended up making my own using a mx of real touch and silks.&amp;nbsp; I did have some dusty miller in my bouquet to match the boutonniere and corsage but ended up taking it out at the last minute as the bouquet was starting to look too busy.&lt;em&gt; &lt;\/em&gt;I purchased the flowers from Michaels and&amp;nbsp;various sellers on Etsy. If anyone is interested in specific flowers from my bouquet send me a message and&amp;nbsp;I&#039;ll tell you where I bought them.&amp;nbsp;All though my bouquet didn&#039;t turn out how I originally envisioned overall I&#039;m pleased with the final result but worried that they might look fake in the pictures. Would love to get some feedback from you ladies. Do they look too fake? Is there anything you would do differently?&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[{"Id":34880,"Name":"P1020506.jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_01_2016\/post-284050-0-22874200-1453812730.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_01_2016\/post-284050-0-22874200-1453812730_thumb.jpg","Width":900,"Height":1200},{"Id":34881,"Name":"P1020507.jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_01_2016\/post-284050-0-33249300-1453812766.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_01_2016\/post-284050-0-33249300-1453812766_thumb.jpg","Width":900,"Height":1200},{"Id":34882,"Name":"P1020512.jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_01_2016\/post-284050-0-28303700-1453812816.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_01_2016\/post-284050-0-28303700-1453812816_thumb.jpg","Width":900,"Height":1200},{"Id":34883,"Name":"P1020513.jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_01_2016\/post-284050-0-18780300-1453812845.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_01_2016\/post-284050-0-18780300-1453812845_thumb.jpg","Width":900,"Height":1200},{"Id":34884,"Name":"P1020522.jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_01_2016\/post-284050-0-95026400-1453812872.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_01_2016\/post-284050-0-95026400-1453812872_thumb.jpg","Width":900,"Height":1200},{"Id":34885,"Name":"P1020523.jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_01_2016\/post-284050-0-46733300-1453812899.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_01_2016\/post-284050-0-46733300-1453812899_thumb.jpg","Width":900,"Height":1200}],"Id":1910048,"PostDate":1453795002,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>I'm leaving for my wedding at Secrets Wild Orchid in MoBay in 2 days and have finally finished my bouquet, my FH's boutonniere and my grandmothers corsage. I would have loved to have real flowers but I wanted peonies in different shades of coral for my bouquet and as many of you know the prices are crazy expensive (quotes I received were in the $600 range just for my bouquet!) to me that is just too expensive for flowers I can't bring home through customs to have as a keepsake so I ended up making my own using a mx of real touch and silks.\u00a0 I did have some dusty miller in my bouquet to match the boutonniere and corsage but ended up taking it out at the last minute as the bouquet was starting to look too busy.<em> <\/em>I purchased the flowers from Michaels and\u00a0various sellers on Etsy. If anyone is interested in specific flowers from my bouquet send me a message and\u00a0I'll tell you where I bought them.\u00a0All though my bouquet didn't turn out how I originally envisioned overall I'm pleased with the final result but worried that they might look fake in the pictures. Would love to get some feedback from you ladies. Do they look too fake? Is there anything you would do differently?<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"webgrl74@gmail.com","IpAddress":"99.224.73.70","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1437418985,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"2ndTimeMrs","Id":284050,"Name":"2ndTimeMrs","IsOnline":true}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":1,"TotalPages":1,"CurrentPage":0,"NextPage":-1,"PreviousPage":-1,"LastPage":0},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":1,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
