{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Id":136875,"Title":"liked a post you made in Ashhtayy's Planning Thr...","Message":"Hello!\n\nashhtayy just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\nha @  You and I have the same taste, but in reverse! @  I vote #2 first then #4  Guys just don't follow flowers.... lol\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79377-ashhtayys-planning-thread-azul-fives-june-7-2016\/?view=findpost&p=1910041\n","Sender":{"Id":282006,"Name":"ashhtayy","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-282006.jpg?_r=1451447049","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":210,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":true},"NotificationDate":1453794857,"IsRead":false,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136865,"Title":"has replied to a personal conversation","Message":"acw271011,\n\nmaybeoneday has replied to a personal conversation entitled \"Something to think about\".\n\nmaybeoneday said:\n======================================================================\nHi Ann, Sounds wonderful! More info would be great! Bal really wants to go back to Mexico but we are just considering plans as we want to move as well. Will have a chat with him once we know more! \n\nPs cannot find anything on FB re Brides trip....I have sent you a message on there xx\n\nMaybeoneday\n14 \/10\/2015 - R R C, Mexico\n======================================================================\n\nPLEASE DO NOT REPLY DIRECTLY TO THIS EMAIL!\nYou can reply to this personal conversation by following the link below:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php?app=members&module=messaging&section=view&do=findMessage&topicID=12636&msgID=__firstUnread__\n","Sender":{"Id":281816,"Name":"maybeoneday","Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453772792,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Conversation","RelatedItemId":12636},{"Id":136792,"Title":"liked a post you made in 2016 Iberostar Rose Hall Su...","Message":"Hello!\n\nKyla0808 just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\nCongrats! Jamaica is a gorgeous place to get married and is quite popular with brides. I'm a 2011 Jamaica bride and we loved it.\n \nGood luck and happy planning!\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79715-2016-iberostar-rose-hall-suites-brides\/?view=findpost&p=1907225\n","Sender":{"Id":285471,"Name":"Kyla0808","Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453750512,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136762,"Title":"has replied to a personal conversation","Message":"acw271011,\n\n2ndTimeMrs has replied to a personal conversation entitled \"Feeling discouraged....need advice\".\n\n2ndTimeMrs said:\n======================================================================\nGood morning Ann - Hope you had a great weekend. I saw your message Friday after work but after a few days of feeling sorry for myself last week I was behind the eight ball for last minute wedding prep so needed to get caught up. After scrambling for the last couple of days I figured I'd come back to work for a break <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> I finished my bouquet, Peter's boutonniere and my Grandmother's corsage late last night so once I get home tonight I will post pictures on here.\n \nOk it's really starting to get scary how similar we are. I am originally from Toronto too (Mississauga to be exact) I've lived in Ottawa since 1998 but like you I hate the city. It's so funny because everyone always says how cold and unfriendly Toronto is but I don't find that at all. I have travelling coast to coast several times and can honestly say Ottawa is the most unfriendly city I've been to in Canada. When my marriage fell apart I was actually going to pick up and move to Bermuda as I had several clients there at the time but by the time I sold my house and got my ducks in a row Peter came along and well the rest is history.\n \nWe're also wine lovers too. Have you and Doug ever been to Prince Edward County near Picton? If you haven't I highly recommend it for a weekend getaway. It's like Niagara where there are tons of wineries. Before we bought our boat a few years ago we used to spend most of our weekends in the summer months there touring all the wineries and adding to our collection -some weekends we were luck if any bottles made it home full <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/laugh.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':lol:' \/>\n \nSorry about your PATS this past weekend. We're both Cheeseheads so we had our hearts broken when Green Bay got defeated the weekend before last by Arizona. We're excited to watch Super Bowl 50  on then beach though. I even had a Packers \"wedding\" Jersey made with the number 2 (for our wedding date) and my new last name (Hallinan).  \n \nI found it really hard too when everyone we invited started dropping out and the younger girls on here were posting their reviews saying things like \"we only had 30 people....etc\" Part of me would love to have a large group and be able to do a lot of the great ideas I've seen other brides do on here but like you said I did that already when I was in my 20's. I had a big wedding last time and look how that turned out. The wedding is only one day...the marriage is forever. We didn't want a big fuss either so in the end we got what we wanted.(I could have done without all the stress in between though)\n \n \nOriginally I was against doing a AHR simply because I felt very bitter about everyone cancelling with obvious made up excuses or not even acknowledging the wedding invitation at all but now that we are getting closer to our wedding day everyone keeps saying when we come home they want to take us out to dinner. In an effort to avoid becoming 500lbs for all the meals out we decided we are going to pick our favorite restaurant in Ottawa and tell everyone where and when we are going. Those who want to come with come and those who don't oh well. We also don't want our wedding drawn out over months of people taking us out to congratulate us so we are going to make it clear to everyone what our wishes are and we are holding firm on them.\n \nI hear ya about the resort not caring. Ever since I reduced my package (AKA how much $$ I'm bringing into the resort) The service level has gone way down. Secrets doesn't have reservations for dinner in their a la cartes but I know from having been there before that the French restaurant does require reservations if you want to sit inside. It is the nicest restaurant and I figured since we were just 6 people (before our witnesses had to cancel) this would be a nice compromise for our wedding reception. I contacted the restaurant booking team to see about reserving a table and they said the resort does not allow people to do that. I have to fight back and forth with them several times saying I was a past customer and I know they take reservations blah, blah, blah.... but they still wouldn't do it. It took me sending them a trip advisor review I found from another bride where she talks about booking a reservation at the restaurant for her FH and parents to have a pre-wedding dinner. Suddenly they were very accommodating. Same goes for the photographer. All the Secrets wedding packages have their photographer for 1 hour. We didn't know we were getting married that last time we were in Jamaica but we wanted nice pictures together so we hired their photographer to take our photos and quite frankly I've seen better photos taken at the Sears Portrait Studio. That's why we hired Misha Earle. The resort was still insisting their photographer has to also take pictures at our wedding and I had to be firm with them. They tried to push me but then I reminded them that I had to pay them $380 for the \"privilege\" to bring in an outside vendor and that if their photographer attends my wedding and hinders our photographer's work then I will not be paying the vendor fee. Suddenly they backed off <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/wink.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=';)' \/>\n \n \nWell I guess I should get back to work!\n \n-Nancy\n \n \n\n------------ QUOTE ----------\nHi Nancy,\n \nIt's nice to e-meet you!!  Oh my goodness - your message gave me chills!!  It's totally unbelievable how many similarities there are between us!!! It's a bit freaky!! lol  First of all, I'm Toronto born but I spent about half of my life or a bit more in Ottawa, then came back to Toronto about 17 years ago when my marriage fell apart. Too many bad memories, and to be truthful I hate the place with a  passion. lol I can totally relate on the good cry!! I've had quite a few of those over the years, and yes - a couple that nearly cost me my relationship with Doug over our wedding plans! So don't ever underestimate the power of a good cry but don't let others force you into one that isn't a \"good\" one!!!\n \nYou're leaving for Jamaica from Toronto, driving from Ottawa next week and next weekend we're going to Ottawa! We have 2 granddaughters there so with so much going on we have one that we still have to do Christmas with, hopefully next weekend, weather permitting! This time of the year it's so unpredictable with snow storms along the lake!\n \nYou're absolutely right about the difference between getting married and having a wedding. And you do get caught up in it. You're on a \"happy\" cloud. I think we got into the same trap as you. When we decided to get married (we didn't have an \"engagement\" really, for specific reasons) and told everyone that we were doing it in Jamaica, it was the same reaction - \"Oh we're going\" and \"It's a good chance for a family vacation\" etc etc. Yeah and we know how that worked out. We didn't want kids at our wedding and that complicated things. Our kids are grown and our grandkids were all babies then so we knew our kids wouldn't have a proper vacation dealing with small children, or I wouldn't so Doug put his foot down and said no kids. Then as people dropped out, the others were worried about paying more for the trip so they dropped out. In the end we had the last laugh because we ended up booking last minute and saved $300 each!\n \nIt was the wedding coordinator in Jamaica that helped me get ready and both of them were our witnesses so our marriage license is signed by complete strangers! But hey - it is what it is and the end result was accomplished, and even now more than 4 years later I still sometimes have to remind myself of that!  Secrets Wild Orchid - nice!!! I've heard so many good reviews of that resort! Are getting married out on the little pier??? It's so pretty!!! I would have loved to go back to Jamaica last October when we did our renewal but we both adore Mexico and hadn't been for several years so it just seemed the obvious choice to go to. We loved it but t's still on the agenda to get back to Jamaica. That was where we were supposed to go for our first anniversary but it was spent in the hospital instead so it's still on the list of \"want to do's\".\n \nI'm sorry to hear about your husband. That's a difficult diagnosis to deal with for sure!!! Yes - life really is too short. We found that out the hard way. By rights I shouldn't be here and thanks to Doug, I am. He's the one that pushed going to the hospital and it's a good thing he did. I used to know someone that was a paid firefighter and I remember he had all kinds of health issues too, and obviously the danger level would bother you!! I can understand that completely! Again, you deal with each day as it comes. Whatever is meant to be is going to be. All you can do is live and love together and hope for the best!!\n \nI had tons of stuff left over too!!!! Omg - that's so funny. I'm a law clerk so it becomes second nature to be organized and always planning so I did the same thing and got everything when everyone said they were going. You made me laugh on the advil, Tylenol and emergen-c. I think we took a year to use stuff up!!! And yes - small groups are of no interest to the resorts so any info is beneficial!! It was difficult in the beginning to see all the \"20 somethngs\" as you called them having their big weddings but I had to stop and think I did that too when I was a 20 something. Doug and I didn't want any fuss, and that's exactly what we got. That's why we ended up having our renewal off site at a restaurant. I tried working with Azul Fives originally and they all want to stick you in an a la carte restaurant with everyone else and that was a no go for me. In the end what we had was perfect! We were 10 for dinner thanks to our planner and her assistant,  husband and daughter plus our photographer and his gf so it worked out fine.\n \nSuper bowl!! That's so cool you get to celebrate it on the beach!!! Who are your teams???? Doug is a Steelers fan and I'm a PATS fan so I've got a lot riding on this weekend!!! Another thing that is so similar! Freaky!! lol We went to a pre-season Steelers-Bills game in August since we live so close to the border so Doug got to see his team in action. He also got me tickets to a PATS Bills game a few Christmases ago, on Boxing Day no less. It was about -30 and we froze our butts off!! lol But it was SOOOOOOO awesome!! I loved it!! We're still trying to organize a Steelers\/PATS game which will happen one of these days!! Doug took me to Gillette Stadium on our way back from his parents for Xmas a year ago so I went camera crazy, plus we did the museum. I got Xmas money and spent it on Brady stuff and stickers for my truck. lol Yes - we're football geeks!!!!\n \nWe're off wine tasting this weekend and it's time to leave the office so I better finish this up and get out of here. Let me know how things are going before you leave if you have time. If not, have a wonderful wedding week and a magical wedding day!! I'm looking forward to seeing the photos!!!\n \nAll the best. Have a good weekend!\nAnn\n-----------------------------\n\n \n======================================================================\n\nPLEASE DO NOT REPLY DIRECTLY TO THIS EMAIL!\nYou can reply to this personal conversation by following the link below:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php?app=members&module=messaging&section=view&do=findMessage&topicID=12571&msgID=__firstUnread__\n","Sender":{"Id":284050,"Name":"2ndTimeMrs","Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"IsOnline":true},"NotificationDate":1453720970,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Conversation","RelatedItemId":12571},{"Id":136717,"Title":"mentioned you in this post","Message":"Hello!\n\nThis message is to notify you that yycbride2016 mentioned you in a post.\n\nThe post that you were mentioned in can be found here:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79227-yycbride2016-grand-sirenis-planning-thread-february-2016\/?view=findpost&p=1909993\n\n----------------------------------\nAhh thanks @\"acw271011\" I really didn't want to spend much on dresses. All together these two dresses totaled at $40! I'm a bargain hunter haha. I ended up wearing a brand new gold dress from winners to my bachelorette. I will post pics. It only cost $21 as it was on a crazy discount! \n\nThanks for the spelling catch ladies @\"vancouverpetunia\". I will fix that ASAP before they all get printed!! \n\nUpdate:\n\nSo we've got a couple things done but not much really. We have all of our rental items booked for our AHR and we also did an IKEA shopping trip to get a few items for the event. So at least that is done and done! \n\nKyle is looking into our sound equipment needs for the atr as well! \n\nWe are also looking into honeymoon options. Everything is crazy at the moment with the exchange rate. We were going to book Hawaii but the prices got insane with the exchange rate so we cancelled that option. We really want to do Costa Rica but it's also quite expensive. We are back looking at some high end resorts in Mexico now. I didn't want to do Mexico two times this year but it might be all we can afford. Plus I'm being a princess and wants 10 day holiday haha. \n\nThe Dress! I picked up my dress Thursday after work. It fits perfectly. It's a little strange in the chest because I actually have a super small chest so she sewed in cups and now I have a boob job without the price tag or surgery hahaha. But it fits and I'm happy! The lighting in these photos doesn't compliment it at all but you get the point.   \n\nBachelorette Party!!! \n\nMy bachelorette party was last night! It was so much fun! We were about 10 girls at my sisters condo. She hired a makeup artist to come in and teach everyone how to do their makeup! And I had my full makeup done for me! It was amazing!! I loved the pampering. We also played loads of bridal games like how well do you know your groom, how well does everyone know the bride, read the brides mind, help the bride write her vows mad libs (super funny and dirty), and so on! It was a blast! Got to see some friends I Hadn't  seen in forever which was so nice! Everyone got prizes and little spa gift bags at the end! It was so cute and my sister did an amazing job! Now I can't wait for my bridal shower in two weeks!! Here are a few photos! \nEveryone doing their makeup:\n \nMy before and after:\n \nMy amazing sister and I:\n \n \n\nKyle is celebrating his bachelor party next weekend. They are renting golf simulators and watching he NHL all stars competition, drinking beer and eating pizza! Sounds exactly like kyles perfect bro-night! I'm sure he will love it! \n\nHopefully this week I will tackle the welcome packages, photo booth items, and take a stab at my vows! \n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\n----------------------------------\n\nIf you no longer wish to receive notifications of posts you are mentioned in, you can adjust your preferences on the\ncommunity by clicking My Settings, and then choosing Notification Options.\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php\n\n","Sender":{"Id":283167,"Name":"yycbride2016","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-283167.jpg?_r=1432133572","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":133,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453677082,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136676,"Title":"liked a post you made in Vancouverpetunia - Now Sapp...","Message":"Hello!\n\nvancouverpetunia just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\n@  I think you should stick with that belt! lol It looks beautiful! LOVE the shoes!! They'll be perfect! I don't think the colour will be any kind of an issue. If anything a slight difference in the shade will set off both really nicely!! A hairband will be so pretty, especially if you get it...\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79068-vancouverpetunia-now-sapphire-april-7-2016\/?view=findpost&p=1909978\n","Sender":{"Id":281283,"Name":"vancouverpetunia","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281283.jpg?_r=1428779369","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453663321,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136649,"Title":"mentioned you in this post","Message":"Hello!\n\nThis message is to notify you that vancouverpetunia mentioned you in a post.\n\nThe post that you were mentioned in can be found here:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79068-vancouverpetunia-now-sapphire-april-7-2016\/?view=findpost&p=1909976\n\n----------------------------------\n@\"rebeccarpeck\", @\"krystalball\" Thank you!  <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\n \n@\"acw271011\" I do like that belt. I actually wouldn't have picked it off the rack - a bit too much bling for me, but I think it looks good. I'm going to hunt around a bit, but may end up getting it. No veil... thinking a headband, which I might try to match to the belt (i.e. if I go with a rhinestone belt, go with a rhinestone headband). The shoes are these:\n   They are a little more ivory than the dress, but I don't think you will notice since there is quite a gap between the dress and the shoes. I don't know if I would have picked them to go with this dress (I picked them to go with a different dress), but I think they'll work. I'll probably end up in flipflops later anyhow  <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/biggrin.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':D' \/>\n----------------------------------\n\nIf you no longer wish to receive notifications of posts you are mentioned in, you can adjust your preferences on the\ncommunity by clicking My Settings, and then choosing Notification Options.\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php\n\n","Sender":{"Id":281283,"Name":"vancouverpetunia","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281283.jpg?_r=1428779369","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453655601,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136644,"Title":"liked a post you made in Vancouverpetunia - Now Sapp...","Message":"Hello!\n\nvancouverpetunia just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\n@  Oh Erin! It's beautiful!!! I really love it!!! It looks gorgeous on you!!!! I think it will be perfect for your wedding!! You're right - it fits perfectly and it definitely needs a belt!! Are you adding that one, or looking for a different one? That one looks great with it!! What are you pu...\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79068-vancouverpetunia-now-sapphire-april-7-2016\/?view=findpost&p=1909975\n","Sender":{"Id":281283,"Name":"vancouverpetunia","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281283.jpg?_r=1428779369","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453655398,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136621,"Title":"liked a post you made in Toronto (Gta) Brides Meet U...","Message":"Hello!\n\nTinkerSofi just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\n------------ QUOTE ----------\nCould everyone please pass me their fb names? I'll put the group together <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\n-----------------------------\n\n \nHey Sof - I already did it but I don't have all of the names. I'll messa...\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79202-toronto-gta-brides-meet-up\/?view=findpost&p=1909968\n","Sender":{"Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1442890536","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453653053,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136619,"Title":"has replied to a personal conversation","Message":"acw271011,\n\nvancouverpetunia has replied to a personal conversation entitled \"Brides Group\".\n\nvancouverpetunia said:\n======================================================================\nHaha... we were on the same wave length at the same time <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\n \n\n------------ QUOTE ----------\nHi Erin,\n \nI'm sorry I'm a bit behind with getting everyone in the loop on the trip we've been talking about, but it just happened so fast! Perian is the one that just threw it out there the other day (Thursday) and it was just a goofy idea. But it sort of caught and as you can see from the postings it just came together literally 2 days ago.\n \nI did the facebook group last night but I'm missing a bunch of ladies to add. I don't have you on my FB so I'll leave it up to you how you would like to do it. Either send me your fb contact or search BDW Brides Trip Group and just ask to join. I set it up so that any of the members can approve anyone to join so it doesn't even have to be me. We've been in Niagara Falls all weekend and just got home a little while ago so I'm trying to get this up to date now.\n \nCheers.\nAnn\n-----------------------------\n\n \n======================================================================\n\nPLEASE DO NOT REPLY DIRECTLY TO THIS EMAIL!\nYou can reply to this personal conversation by following the link below:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php?app=members&module=messaging&section=view&do=findMessage&topicID=12620&msgID=__firstUnread__\n","Sender":{"Id":281283,"Name":"vancouverpetunia","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281283.jpg?_r=1428779369","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453652961,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Conversation","RelatedItemId":12620},{"Id":136618,"Title":"has replied to a personal conversation","Message":"acw271011,\n\nTinkerSofi has replied to a personal conversation entitled \"Brides Group\".\n\nTinkerSofi said:\n======================================================================\ngreat! It's Sofia Lopez. You might find a lot of us haha, my profile pic is us on the wedding day on the sea pier at AF <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> \n======================================================================\n\nPLEASE DO NOT REPLY DIRECTLY TO THIS EMAIL!\nYou can reply to this personal conversation by following the link below:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php?app=members&module=messaging&section=view&do=findMessage&topicID=12618&msgID=__firstUnread__\n","Sender":{"Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1442890536","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453652825,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Conversation","RelatedItemId":12618},{"Id":136615,"Title":"started a new personal conversation with you","Message":"acw271011,\n\nvancouverpetunia has sent you a new personal conversation entitled \"Facebook Group\".\n\nvancouverpetunia said:\n======================================================================\nHi Ann,\n \nCan you please me add me to the FB group for the BDW bride reunion trip? <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> You'll find me as Erin Kampf.\n \nThanks,\nErin\n======================================================================\n\nPLEASE DO NOT REPLY DIRECTLY TO THIS EMAIL!\nYou can reply to this personal conversation by following the link below:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php?app=members&module=messaging&section=view&do=showConversation&topicID=12619#msg22113\n","Sender":{"Id":281283,"Name":"vancouverpetunia","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281283.jpg?_r=1428779369","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453652595,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Conversation","RelatedItemId":12619},{"Id":136598,"Title":"liked a post you made in Toronto (Gta) Brides Meet U...","Message":"Hello!\n\nTinkerSofi just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\nAhhhhhh !! Wow!! Ladies do you think this might actually come together????? This is so totally cool!! So I've had umm \"some\" wine.... so I'll take a stab at this.@  @  @  @  @  @  @  ........ I know I'm forgetting people.  I would absolutely be up for Cancun for same reason as Kim - I've never...\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79202-toronto-gta-brides-meet-up\/?view=findpost&p=1909944\n","Sender":{"Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1442890536","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453649864,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136585,"Title":"mentioned you in this post","Message":"Hello!\n\nThis message is to notify you that vancouverpetunia mentioned you in a post.\n\nThe post that you were mentioned in can be found here:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79068-vancouverpetunia-now-sapphire-april-7-2016\/?view=findpost&p=1909961\n\n----------------------------------\nSo I picked up my dress last night and I couldn't be happier [emoji4] It's not exactly the same as the photo but it's similar and I think it's very pretty. It is also beautiful work(wo)manship. And it fits like a glove! Not a gap or a pucker anywhere. \n\n \n\nThe belt doesn't come with with it, but it definitely needs one. \n\n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\n@\"acw271011\" Thanks, Ann, for you suggestions, feedback & support! [emoji4]\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\n----------------------------------\n\nIf you no longer wish to receive notifications of posts you are mentioned in, you can adjust your preferences on the\ncommunity by clicking My Settings, and then choosing Notification Options.\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php\n\n","Sender":{"Id":281283,"Name":"vancouverpetunia","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281283.jpg?_r=1428779369","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453643219,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136515,"Title":"liked a post you made in Toronto (Gta) Brides Meet U...","Message":"Hello!\n\ncalgarybride2015 just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\nAhhhhhh !! Wow!! Ladies do you think this might actually come together????? This is so totally cool!! So I've had umm \"some\" wine.... so I'll take a stab at this.@  @  @  @  @  @  @  ........ I know I'm forgetting people.  I would absolutely be up for Cancun for same reason as Kim - I've never...\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79202-toronto-gta-brides-meet-up\/?view=findpost&p=1909944\n","Sender":{"Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453571277,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136510,"Title":"liked a post you made in Toronto (Gta) Brides Meet U...","Message":"Hello!\n\nperianjay just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\nAhhhhhh !! Wow!! Ladies do you think this might actually come together????? This is so totally cool!! So I've had umm \"some\" wine.... so I'll take a stab at this.@  @  @  @  @  @  @  ........ I know I'm forgetting people.  I would absolutely be up for Cancun for same reason as Kim - I've never...\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79202-toronto-gta-brides-meet-up\/?view=findpost&p=1909944\n","Sender":{"Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1453235488","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453570445,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136378,"Title":"liked a post you made in Toronto (Gta) Brides Meet U...","Message":"Hello!\n\ndeecol just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\n@perianjay  Oh I'm going to take a look at that!! The hard part is trying to get a handle on price points. But I'm going to check it out.\n \nBabies!! Omg I never even thought about that..... lmao  Just shows you where my head is at with kids! lol Doug and I have done...\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79202-toronto-gta-brides-meet-up\/?view=findpost&p=1909911\n","Sender":{"Id":281751,"Name":"deecol","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281751.jpg?_r=1443808962","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453535286,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136366,"Title":"liked a post you made in Toronto (Gta) Brides Meet U...","Message":"Hello!\n\nashhtayy just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\n@perianjay  Oh I'm going to take a look at that!! The hard part is trying to get a handle on price points. But I'm going to check it out.\n \nBabies!! Omg I never even thought about that..... lmao  Just shows you where my head is at with kids! lol Doug and I have done...\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79202-toronto-gta-brides-meet-up\/?view=findpost&p=1909911\n","Sender":{"Id":282006,"Name":"ashhtayy","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-282006.jpg?_r=1451447049","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":210,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":true},"NotificationDate":1453511761,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136360,"Title":"liked a post you made in Toronto (Gta) Brides Meet U...","Message":"Hello!\n\nperianjay just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\n@perianjay  Oh I'm going to take a look at that!! The hard part is trying to get a handle on price points. But I'm going to check it out.\n \nBabies!! Omg I never even thought about that..... lmao  Just shows you where my head is at with kids! lol Doug and I have done...\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79202-toronto-gta-brides-meet-up\/?view=findpost&p=1909911\n","Sender":{"Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1453235488","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453508743,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136301,"Title":"liked a post you made in Deecol's Planning Threa...","Message":"Hello!\n\nperianjay just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\n@deecol  LOVE the bouquet! You totally rocked it with those little flowers, and the bout too!! They'll be gorgeous in your photos!!  (hope the tea was tetley, or something else as good! not the horrible stuff you buy here!)\n \nYay to double digits!!\n <p...\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/?view=findpost&p=1909881\n","Sender":{"Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1453235488","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453453124,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136292,"Title":"mentioned you in this post","Message":"Hello!\n\nThis message is to notify you that deecol mentioned you in a post.\n\nThe post that you were mentioned in can be found here:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/?view=findpost&p=1909890\n\n----------------------------------\n@\"acw271011\" Thanks Ann!  I love the way they turned out, those little flowers really finished them off.  haha I was drinking a tea from David's tea, I'm slightly addicted to that place.\n \n@calgarybride2015 @\"acw271011\" @\"ashhtayy\" omg double digits!  It came so fast!\n \n@\"ashhtayy\" I feel like I still have a million things to do but I'm glad I look composed and accomplished on the outside lol!   So much fun stuff happening!  My bridal shower is in 2 weeks... and then it's just going to fly from there!\n----------------------------------\n\nIf you no longer wish to receive notifications of posts you are mentioned in, you can adjust your preferences on the\ncommunity by clicking My Settings, and then choosing Notification Options.\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php\n\n","Sender":{"Id":281751,"Name":"deecol","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281751.jpg?_r=1443808962","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453450933,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136287,"Title":"liked a post you made in Deecol's Planning Threa...","Message":"Hello!\n\ndeecol just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\n@deecol  LOVE the bouquet! You totally rocked it with those little flowers, and the bout too!! They'll be gorgeous in your photos!!  (hope the tea was tetley, or something else as good! not the horrible stuff you buy here!)\n \nYay to double digits!!\n <p...\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/?view=findpost&p=1909881\n","Sender":{"Id":281751,"Name":"deecol","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281751.jpg?_r=1443808962","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453450751,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136276,"Title":"has replied to a personal conversation","Message":"acw271011,\n\n2ndTimeMrs has replied to a personal conversation entitled \"Feeling discouraged....need advice\".\n\n2ndTimeMrs said:\n======================================================================\nHi Ann - Thank you so much for the pep talk and advice it really did help me feel better\u2026.a darn good cry didn\u2019t hurt either <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\n I couldn\u2019t imagine having to go through this twice I feel so bad for you but glad to hear that you and Doug stuck it out and survived as a couple through it all. I think the issue started for us when we first got engaged and everyone was so excited for us and said they just had to be there. We both got wrapped up in that and veered away from what we had originally wanted\u2026to get married; not have a wedding. To me there is a difference.\nFunny you should mention being upset about not having anyone there to help you get ready. That was one of the first things I thought of when our friends cancelled the other day. At first I told myself I was being self-absorbed but then I thought really no I wasn\u2019t, I'm the bride; I deserve my bridal moment\u2026.then I had a good cry. I know my grandmother will be there and she would help me but I really want the first time she sees me in my dress to be when I walk down the aisle so I will probably just get the resort wedding coordinator to help me get dressed.\nSorry to hear your son lost all his money on the cancelled trip. Our witnesses that just cancelled the other day also lost most of their money and since they had a completely valid reason we felt so bad for them.\nYou and Doug have definitely been through hell and back with all your medical issues. We can also relate to that. I am relatively healthy (knock on wood) but about a week and half ago Peter was pre-diagnosed by his doctor as having early onset Parkinson\u2019s disease. I have suspected that for a while as he has demonstrated the symptoms for quite some time (uncontrolled movements, headaches) but we won\u2019t know for sure until we get back as he needs to go for neurological tests before the doctor can say for sure. I am devastated inside but staying strong on the outside for Peter\u2019s sake. When something like this happens it really puts everything else in perspective and makes you realize life it too short. I told myself yesterday that at least we are lucky to have found each other and are both still here to love each other. Peter has also been a volunteer firefighter for about 28 years so he has all kinds of medical issues related to being on the job for that long. And with him being a firefighter he is constantly putting himself in danger and I never know if when he runs out the door it will be the last time I see him.\nWe had a long talk last night and decided enough was enough with trying to please other people when it\u2019s supposed to be our day. We\u2019ve booked a day of golf at White Witch Golf Club on the day before our wedding and are trying to coordinate with the resort right now to have a special candlelight dinner on the beach or one of teh gazebos on the evening of our wedding for just the two of us. Hopefully they can make it happen but if they don\u2019t then we will find another way to make it special. And I know you are right, once we\u2019re there and relaxed on vacation we will feel better and forget about how much disappointment in our friends and family we feel right now.\nOf course being the organized planner that I am I prepared most the wedding stuff (programs, gift bags, etc) a long time ago before we knew everyone was not coming so I have all these things ready with no one to give them to other than my grandparents. On the plus side I have enough Tylenol, Advil and emergen-c to survive the apocalypse <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/laugh.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':lol:' \/>\n We have a wonderful photographer, Misha Earle, and she has been so fantastic so far. We had a skype session with her around Christmas and we had a great connection with her so we\u2019re looking forward to have her capture our day so we have some beautiful memories to look back on. I will definitely share pictures. I\u2019m also planning to write a review of the resort (Secrets Wild Orchid) and other vendors we dealt with as well as tips for other brides no matter what resort they are getting married at. I also plan to focus on information for brides planning small weddings as I found there is lack of that on here. It seems like most brides end up have big groups and I guess if you are 20 something and it is your first wedding you get a better turn out then someone middle aged getting remarried. (We\u2019re in our mid to late 40s so we are only about a decade behind you and Doug in age)\nThanks again for the kind words everything you said really did help me feel better and put everything into perspective. I still had a few moments of sadness today but can feel the pain fading away now that I\u2019ve decided to move forward and not let these speed bumps ruin our day.\nWe live on Ottawa but are flying out of Toronto so will be driving to Toronto next Thursday (28th) and we fly out the morning of the 29th. Our wedding is on the 2nd and we are staying for 10 days so won\u2019t be coming back home until the evening of the 8th. We actually planned it that way because we were expecting all these people to come for 7 days and figured 10 days would give us a few days to ourselves plus we are both big football fans and the Super Bowl in on February 7th this year so our last night at the resort will be celebrated with a big Super Bowl party the Secrets Wild Orchid has on the beach every year. Will be a fun way to end what will be a beautiful wedding vacation.\nWarmest regards-\nNancy\n \n\n------------ QUOTE ----------\nOh my goodness - I'm so sorry you're going through all of this. I can completely relate and totally sympathize! We went through the same thing! Twice!! So I know what you're going through.\n \nThe same thing happened to us when we got married in Jamaica. The wedding coordinators signed our marriage license and then when we renewed our vows in October in Mexico, it happened again almost the same. At least that time we did have a couple that went with us (there's a link to our photos posted on my Mexico thread and a link to our video) but my son cancelled 5 days before departure and lost all the money that had been paid.\n \nI wish I had some wonderful advice. i don't. It is so disappointing. We originally were supposed to be around 16 for our wedding 4 years ago and one by one, everyone had an excuse. In the end, people dropped out because they were afraid that the cost would get jacked up with losing the group rate. It very nearly split Doug and I up. In fact the couple that were our MOH and BM booked another holiday because they were so sure we were done so needless to say they backed out too.\n \nI'm going to be very, very honest. It was tough. i cried when I realized I wouldn't have anyone to help me with my dress, or to sit and get hair and makeup done with. It was Doug that put the right spin on it. Everyone tried forcing us into having a wedding here at home and we went through the motions of looking at locations and checking menus and all that other stuff. But Doug wasn't happy doing it and I was getting more frustrated. He is the one that said flat out - do you want to marry me or not? Of course I said absolutely. Then he asked me what was more important - marrying him or having a wedding. When I said marrying him, he said fine. We're going to Jamaica. So we did and the resort did everything they could to make it super special. Our photographer stayed and had dinner with us (you're supposed to feed them anyway if you have them for a certain amount of time), then we just went to the piano bar after dinner and had a few dances. Sometimes I still wish we had people there with us but with everything else we've been through since we got married, it just isn't important anymore. I nearly died right before our first wedding anniversary, which was spent in the hospital and then our 3rd anniversary was also spent in the hospital. It's why we renewed our vows. I'm still here to be married to Doug and that means more than anything.\n \nIn the end we had a small at home reception 2 weeks after we got married and everyone that was supposed to go to Jamaica was there. We had a great time and ran a slide show of our wedding. It wasn't perfect but 4 years later I can say it is what it is. I married the love of my life on a beautiful beach in Jamaica. What more can you really ask for? And you do really have 2 people going with you. You need to find the positive where you can and appreciate the fact that they're willing to travel with you.\n \nOnce you're there and doing the resort stuff and actually getting ready for your wedding, a lot of it fades away because you're focused on other things. I don't know if an AHR is an option for you or not, but it did help take some of the disappointment away because there were people there that did make a fuss over us and genuinely seemed happy for us. Plus, Doug's parents ended up giving us the money they would have spent on the trip as a wedding gift.\n \nI don't know if any of this helps or not. It's something you can't change so you just have to go with it. I think if you can get that idea into your head and focus on the positive, it will still be special and beautiful. I hope you have a photographer and will post pics! I would love to see! Which resort are you going to and what date do you leave?\n \nAll the best,\nAnn\nPS - I'm going to be 58 in a couple of months and Doug will be 59 later this year so we're definitely a lot older than the average \"bride\" here! lol\n-----------------------------\n======================================================================\n\nPLEASE DO NOT REPLY DIRECTLY TO THIS EMAIL!\nYou can reply to this personal conversation by following the link below:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php?app=members&module=messaging&section=view&do=findMessage&topicID=12571&msgID=__firstUnread__\n","Sender":{"Id":284050,"Name":"2ndTimeMrs","Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"IsOnline":true},"NotificationDate":1453443828,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Conversation","RelatedItemId":12571},{"Id":136229,"Title":"mentioned you in this post","Message":"Hello!\n\nThis message is to notify you that snswedding2016 mentioned you in a post.\n\nThe post that you were mentioned in can be found here:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79202-toronto-gta-brides-meet-up\/?view=findpost&p=1909880\n\n----------------------------------\nhahaha! @\"acw271011\" hence the  <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/blink.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':blink:' \/>  <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/blink.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':blink:' \/>  emoticons ....yea that was my reaction too when I looked it up! It is definitely out of our price range for sure but it is a nice pipe dream! <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/wink.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=';)' \/>\n----------------------------------\n\nIf you no longer wish to receive notifications of posts you are mentioned in, you can adjust your preferences on the\ncommunity by clicking My Settings, and then choosing Notification Options.\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php\n\n","Sender":{"Id":281055,"Name":"snswedding2016","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281055.jpg?_r=1415590512","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453421418,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136222,"Title":"liked a post you made in Toronto (Gta) Brides Meet U...","Message":"Hello!\n\nsnswedding2016 just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\n@  @ . I've heard of it obviously but don't know anything about it. Do you know who flies there? Should I be afraid to look at the price point??? lolOMG!!!! Do you ladies know what you're asking??? lmao Uhhh there is NO WAY I could get Doug to spend that kind of money!! lol I found it for abo...\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79202-toronto-gta-brides-meet-up\/?view=findpost&p=1909879\n","Sender":{"Id":281055,"Name":"snswedding2016","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281055.jpg?_r=1415590512","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453421310,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136215,"Title":"liked a post you made in Toronto (Gta) Brides Meet U...","Message":"Hello!\n\nperianjay just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\n@  @ . I've heard of it obviously but don't know anything about it. Do you know who flies there? Should I be afraid to look at the price point??? lol\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79202-toronto-gta-brides-meet-up\/?view=findpost&p=1909879\n","Sender":{"Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1453235488","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453420440,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136157,"Title":"liked a post you made in Toronto (Gta) Brides Meet U...","Message":"Hello!\n\nperianjay just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\n<blockquote  class=\"ipsBlockquote\" data-author=\"snswedding2016\" data-cid=\"1909866\" data-time=\"1453433819\">@  winter sounds good to me and a year from now will be like a anniversary trip - perfect timing! haha I'm always happy going to Mexico! <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> I'm up for adults only if others are.<\/p...\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79202-toronto-gta-brides-meet-up\/?view=findpost&p=1909867\n","Sender":{"Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1453235488","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453416265,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136150,"Title":"mentioned you in this post","Message":"Hello!\n\nThis message is to notify you that snswedding2016 mentioned you in a post.\n\nThe post that you were mentioned in can be found here:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79202-toronto-gta-brides-meet-up\/?view=findpost&p=1909866\n\n----------------------------------\n@\"acw271011\" winter sounds good to me and a year from now will be like a anniversary trip - perfect timing! haha\n \nI'm always happy going to Mexico! <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> I'm up for adults only if others are. \n----------------------------------\n\nIf you no longer wish to receive notifications of posts you are mentioned in, you can adjust your preferences on the\ncommunity by clicking My Settings, and then choosing Notification Options.\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php\n\n","Sender":{"Id":281055,"Name":"snswedding2016","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281055.jpg?_r=1415590512","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453415819,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136145,"Title":"liked a post you made in Toronto (Gta) Brides Meet U...","Message":"Hello!\n\nperianjay just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\n@snswedding @  I would totally be up for this and I could convince Doug. Tropical? Without question!!!! lolI'm thinking since so many of us have experience with Mexico that's good... Mexico would be a good choice, unless it's a decision to go somewhere different.Second thing I'm thinking is t...\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79202-toronto-gta-brides-meet-up\/?view=findpost&p=1909865\n","Sender":{"Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1453235488","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453415410,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":136129,"Title":"mentioned you in this post","Message":"Hello!\n\nThis message is to notify you that perianjay mentioned you in a post.\n\nThe post that you were mentioned in can be found here:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79202-toronto-gta-brides-meet-up\/?view=findpost&p=1909863\n\n----------------------------------\n@\"snswedding2016\" @\"acw271011\" I'm definitely in for this. I never say no to travel and especially somewhere tropical. Chester and I would be interested for sure <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> we can definitely plan a trip and save until then. I like the idea of looking into a group rate! \n\nI have no real preference for a resort at this point. I'd be happy to go anywhere nice. I'd love  to goto a karisma resort or really any other resort. We definitely should include our west. Coast ladies because I'd love for my sister from another mister to join in @\"Wafflesmom\" and of course @\"calgarybride2015\" and @\"yycbride2016\" <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>  and sorry if I missed any others. I just got home from yoga and I'm focused on my aching back at the moment\n----------------------------------\n\nIf you no longer wish to receive notifications of posts you are mentioned in, you can adjust your preferences on the\ncommunity by clicking My Settings, and then choosing Notification Options.\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php\n\n","Sender":{"Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1453235488","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1453413727,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"","RelatedItemId":0}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":"280","TotalPages":10,"CurrentPage":0,"NextPage":30,"PreviousPage":-1,"LastPage":270},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":1,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
