{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Id":22046,"Author":{"Id":284050,"Name":"2ndTimeMrs","Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"IsOnline":true},"Date":1453303588,"Content":"Hi acw271011 \u2013 I\u2019m about 2 weeks out from my wedding and could really use some words of advice\/wisdom and having read your posts on here I think you may be the best woman for the job.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nLike you and Doug, Peter and I are older, met online, and, getting married in Jamaica. We too fell in love with the country and its people during our first visit a few years ago so when we got engaged we knew we wanted to return to Jamaica to get married. Originally we just wanted to go away, the two of us and maybe another couple to act as witnesses. We\u2019ve both been married before so we were more interested in focusing on the marriage and not the trappings of a big wedding. That all changed when we told everyone we got engaged. All our friends and family insisted they were coming. So away I went with planning a big wedding completed with gift bags for each guest, a catered dinner on the beach, steel drum band and beach bonfire party. I guess you know where this is going.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nI sent the save the date cards in March and the invitations in May so that everyone would have plenty of time to save and plan. Nobody responded for months then around October one by one they all had excuses why they wouldn\u2019t be able to make it.  Several people didn\u2019t even send back their reply cards or even acknowledge our wedding at all (something I know many other brides on BDW have experienced). You said it best in your \u201cnon-planning thread\u201d post\u2026nobody will care as much about your wedding as you do.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nMy Maid of Honor bailed 120 days before the wedding saying her new thyroid medication prevented her from being in the sun. That was partially true but the real reason (I found out later) was that she ordered here bridesmaid dress 6 sizes too small thinking she would lose all kinds of weight on this new medication but she didn\u2019t and didn\u2019t have time to order another dress so she panicked and cancelled with her medical excuse. We each only had a best man and maid of honor and since it was too late for me to ask someone else to step up Peter asked his best man to step down. Turns out his best man was about to cancel anyway as he had work commitments he couldn\u2019t get out of. So we were disappointed but resigned ourselves to not having a wedding party. <br \/>\n<br \/>\nBy our booking cut-off time in December we were left with just my Grandparents and one other couple who were going to be our witnesses. I was very hurt as I had put so much work and time into something that I was really only doing because everyone else wanted it but once I had time to let it soak in I realized it wasn\u2019t all bad as it would allow me to customize the gift bags for each of the four people attending and also not be so hard to coordinate everyone on the day of the wedding. So I contacted the resort changed our package to the basic free wedding package, hired a violinist to play for the ceremony  and cancelled the steel drum band, bonfire and dinner then moved forward with planning a more intimate event for the 6 of us.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nThis brings me to yesterday. Our friends that were coming as our witnesses had to cancel due to some work issues they couldn\u2019t get out of. So now we are left with just us and my Grandparents. I know that I should feel blessed that at their age they can still travel and have chosen to come to our wedding, especially since we are staying at a higher end resort and they are on a fixed income, but I can\u2019t help but feel sad that nobody else cares enough to make the trip especially since they all insisted they had to come.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nI know from your posts that a similar situation happened to you and by the time your wedding came you were left with just the two of you. How did you get through the disappointment? I feel so discouraged and sad right now but I want to get past it because I don\u2019t want to let this ruin our day. I know the most important people will be there (Peter and I) in in the end that\u2019s all that matters but still sad and feeling resentful towards our friends nonetheless.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nSorry for the long winded message. I guess it\u2019s one of those situations that once you open the flood gates it\u2019s hard to close them <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\uf04a<br \/>\n","PostKey":"e237b13b59bbebf8a8f6eda2f204d352","CanDelete":false,"Attachments":[]},{"Id":22061,"Author":{"Id":232000,"Name":"acw271011","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232000.jpg?_r=1434318164","PhotoWidth":570,"PhotoHeight":541,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":true},"Date":1453331384,"Content":"<p>Oh my goodness - I'm so sorry you're going through all of this. I can completely relate and totally sympathize! We went through the same thing! Twice!! So I know what you're going through.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The same thing happened to us when we got married in Jamaica. The wedding coordinators signed our marriage license and then when we renewed our vows in October in Mexico, it happened again almost the same. At least that time we did have a couple that went with us (there's a link to our photos posted on my Mexico thread and a link to our video) but my son cancelled 5 days before departure and lost all the money that had been paid.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I wish I had some wonderful advice. i don't. It is so disappointing. We originally were supposed to be around 16 for our wedding 4 years ago and one by one, everyone had an excuse. In the end, people dropped out because they were afraid that the cost would get jacked up with losing the group rate. It very nearly split Doug and I up. In fact the couple that were our MOH and BM booked another holiday because they were so sure we were done so needless to say they backed out too.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm going to be very, very honest. It was tough. i cried when I realized I wouldn't have anyone to help me with my dress, or to sit and get hair and makeup done with. It was Doug that put the right spin on it. Everyone tried forcing us into having a wedding here at home and we went through the motions of looking at locations and checking menus and all that other stuff. But Doug wasn't happy doing it and I was getting more frustrated. He is the one that said flat out - do you want to marry me or not? Of course I said absolutely. Then he asked me what was more important - marrying him or having a wedding. When I said marrying him, he said fine. We're going to Jamaica. So we did and the resort did everything they could to make it super special. Our photographer stayed and had dinner with us (you're supposed to feed them anyway if you have them for a certain amount of time), then we just went to the piano bar after dinner and had a few dances. Sometimes I still wish we had people there with us but with everything else we've been through since we got married, it just isn't important anymore. I nearly died right before our first wedding anniversary, which was spent in the hospital and then our 3rd anniversary was also spent in the hospital. It's why we renewed our vows. I'm still here to be married to Doug and that means more than anything.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>In the end we had a small at home reception 2 weeks after we got married and everyone that was supposed to go to Jamaica was there. We had a great time and ran a slide show of our wedding. It wasn't perfect but 4 years later I can say it is what it is. I married the love of my life on a beautiful beach in Jamaica. What more can you really ask for? And you do really have 2 people going with you. You need to find the positive where you can and appreciate the fact that they're willing to travel with you.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Once you're there and doing the resort stuff and actually getting ready for your wedding, a lot of it fades away because you're focused on other things. I don't know if an AHR is an option for you or not, but it did help take some of the disappointment away because there were people there that did make a fuss over us and genuinely seemed happy for us. Plus, Doug's parents ended up giving us the money they would have spent on the trip as a wedding gift.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I don't know if any of this helps or not. It's something you can't change so you just have to go with it. I think if you can get that idea into your head and focus on the positive, it will still be special and beautiful. I hope you have a photographer and will post pics! I would love to see! Which resort are you going to and what date do you leave?<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>All the best,<\/p>\n<p>Ann<\/p>\n<p>PS - I'm going to be 58 in a couple of months and Doug will be 59 later this year so we're definitely a lot older than the average \"bride\" here! lol<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n","PostKey":"a752dfeff9fa0c1039203319ffc49387","CanDelete":true,"Attachments":[]},{"Id":22088,"Author":{"Id":284050,"Name":"2ndTimeMrs","Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"IsOnline":true},"Date":1453443828,"Content":"<p>Hi Ann - Thank you so much for the pep talk and advice it really did help me feel better\u2026.a darn good cry didn\u2019t hurt either <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\n\u00a0I couldn\u2019t imagine having to go through this twice I feel so bad for you but glad to hear that you and Doug stuck it out and survived as a couple through it all. I think the issue started for us when we first got engaged and everyone was so excited for us and said they just had to be there. We both got wrapped up in that and veered away from what we had originally wanted\u2026to get married; not have a wedding. To me there is a difference.<\/p>\n<p>\nFunny you should mention being upset about not having anyone there to help you get ready. That was one of the first things I thought of when our friends cancelled the other day. At first I told myself I was being self-absorbed but then I thought\u00a0really no I wasn\u2019t, I'm the bride; I\u00a0deserve my bridal moment\u2026.then I had a good cry. I know my grandmother will be there and she would help me but I really want the first time she sees me in my dress to be when I walk down the aisle so I will probably just get the resort wedding coordinator to help me get dressed.<\/p>\n<p>\nSorry to hear your son lost all his money on the cancelled trip. Our witnesses that just cancelled the other day also lost most of their money and since they had a completely valid reason we felt so bad for them.<\/p>\n<p>\nYou and Doug have definitely been through hell and back with all your medical issues. We can also relate to that. I am relatively healthy (knock on wood) but about a week and half ago Peter was pre-diagnosed by his doctor as having early onset Parkinson\u2019s disease. I have suspected that for a while as he has demonstrated the symptoms for quite some time (uncontrolled movements, headaches) but we won\u2019t know for sure until we get back as he needs to go for neurological tests before the doctor can say for sure. I am devastated inside but staying strong on the outside for Peter\u2019s sake. When something like this happens it really puts everything else in perspective and makes you realize life it too short. I told myself yesterday that at least we are lucky to have found each other and are both still here to love each other. Peter has also been a volunteer firefighter for about 28 years so he has all kinds of medical issues related to being on the job for that long. And with him being a firefighter he is constantly putting himself in danger and I never know if when he runs out the door it will be the last time I see him.<\/p>\n<p>\nWe had a long talk last night and decided enough was enough with trying to please other people when it\u2019s supposed to be our day. We\u2019ve booked a day of golf at White Witch Golf Club on the day before our wedding and are trying to coordinate with the resort right now to have a special candlelight dinner on the beach or one of teh gazebos\u00a0on the evening of our wedding for just the two of us. Hopefully they can make it happen but if they don\u2019t then we will find another way to make it special. And I know you are right, once we\u2019re there and relaxed on vacation we will feel better and forget about how much disappointment in our friends and family we feel right now.<\/p>\n<p>\nOf course being the organized planner that I am I prepared most the wedding stuff (programs, gift bags, etc) a long time ago before we knew everyone was not coming so I have all these things ready with no one to give them to other than my grandparents. On the plus side I have enough Tylenol, Advil and emergen-c to survive the apocalypse <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/laugh.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':lol:' \/><\/p>\n<p>\n\u00a0We have a wonderful photographer, Misha Earle, and she has been so fantastic so far. We had a skype session with her around Christmas and we had a great connection with her so we\u2019re looking forward to have her capture our day so we have some beautiful memories to look back on. I will definitely share pictures. I\u2019m also planning to write a review of the resort (Secrets Wild Orchid) and other vendors we dealt with as well as tips for other brides no matter what resort they are getting married at. I also plan to focus on information for brides planning small weddings as I found there is lack of that on here. It seems like most brides end up have big groups and I guess if you are 20 something and it is your first wedding you get a better turn out then someone middle aged getting remarried. (We\u2019re in our mid to late 40s so we are only about a decade behind you and Doug in age)<\/p>\n<p>\nThanks again for the kind words everything you said really did help me feel better and put everything into perspective. I still had a few moments of sadness today but can feel the pain fading away now that I\u2019ve decided to move forward and not let these speed bumps ruin our day.<br>\nWe live on Ottawa but are flying out of Toronto so will be driving to Toronto next Thursday (28th) and we fly out the morning of the 29th. Our wedding is on the 2nd and we are staying for 10 days so won\u2019t be coming back home until the evening of the 8th. We actually planned it that way because we were expecting all these people to come for 7 days and figured 10 days would give us a few days to ourselves plus we are both big football fans and the Super Bowl in on February 7th this year so our last night at the resort will be celebrated with a big Super Bowl party the Secrets Wild Orchid has on the beach every year. Will be a fun way to end what will be a beautiful wedding vacation.<\/p>\n<p>\nWarmest regards-<br>\nNancy<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<blockquote  class=\"ipsBlockquote\" data-author=\"acw271011\" data-time=\"1453349384\">\n<div>\n<p>Oh my goodness - I'm so sorry you're going through all of this. I can completely relate and totally sympathize! We went through the same thing! Twice!! So I know what you're going through.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The same thing happened to us when we got married in Jamaica. The wedding coordinators signed our marriage license and then when we renewed our vows in October in Mexico, it happened again almost the same. At least that time we did have a couple that went with us (there's a link to our photos posted on my Mexico thread and a link to our video) but my son cancelled 5 days before departure and lost all the money that had been paid.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I wish I had some wonderful advice. i don't. It is so disappointing. We originally were supposed to be around 16 for our wedding 4 years ago and one by one, everyone had an excuse. In the end, people dropped out because they were afraid that the cost would get jacked up with losing the group rate. It very nearly split Doug and I up. In fact the couple that were our MOH and BM booked another holiday because they were so sure we were done so needless to say they backed out too.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm going to be very, very honest. It was tough. i cried when I realized I wouldn't have anyone to help me with my dress, or to sit and get hair and makeup done with. It was Doug that put the right spin on it. Everyone tried forcing us into having a wedding here at home and we went through the motions of looking at locations and checking menus and all that other stuff. But Doug wasn't happy doing it and I was getting more frustrated. He is the one that said flat out - do you want to marry me or not? Of course I said absolutely. Then he asked me what was more important - marrying him or having a wedding. When I said marrying him, he said fine. We're going to Jamaica. So we did and the resort did everything they could to make it super special. Our photographer stayed and had dinner with us (you're supposed to feed them anyway if you have them for a certain amount of time), then we just went to the piano bar after dinner and had a few dances. Sometimes I still wish we had people there with us but with everything else we've been through since we got married, it just isn't important anymore. I nearly died right before our first wedding anniversary, which was spent in the hospital and then our 3rd anniversary was also spent in the hospital. It's why we renewed our vows. I'm still here to be married to Doug and that means more than anything.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>In the end we had a small at home reception 2 weeks after we got married and everyone that was supposed to go to Jamaica was there. We had a great time and ran a slide show of our wedding. It wasn't perfect but 4 years later I can say it is what it is. I married the love of my life on a beautiful beach in Jamaica. What more can you really ask for? And you do really have 2 people going with you. You need to find the positive where you can and appreciate the fact that they're willing to travel with you.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Once you're there and doing the resort stuff and actually getting ready for your wedding, a lot of it fades away because you're focused on other things. I don't know if an AHR is an option for you or not, but it did help take some of the disappointment away because there were people there that did make a fuss over us and genuinely seemed happy for us. Plus, Doug's parents ended up giving us the money they would have spent on the trip as a wedding gift.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I don't know if any of this helps or not. It's something you can't change so you just have to go with it. I think if you can get that idea into your head and focus on the positive, it will still be special and beautiful. I hope you have a photographer and will post pics! I would love to see! Which resort are you going to and what date do you leave?<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>All the best,<\/p>\n<p>Ann<\/p>\n<p>PS - I'm going to be 58 in a couple of months and Doug will be 59 later this year so we're definitely a lot older than the average \"bride\" here! lol<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/blockquote>","PostKey":"eef1ad4ae8b5c31f141a5966c03d7c8b","CanDelete":false,"Attachments":[]},{"Id":22094,"Author":{"Id":232000,"Name":"acw271011","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232000.jpg?_r=1434318164","PhotoWidth":570,"PhotoHeight":541,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":true},"Date":1453482397,"Content":"<p>Hi Nancy,<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>It's nice to e-meet you!!\u00a0 Oh my goodness - your message gave me chills!!\u00a0 It's totally unbelievable how many similarities there are between us!!! It's a bit freaky!! lol\u00a0 First of all, I'm Toronto born but I spent about half of my life or a bit more in Ottawa, then came back to Toronto about 17 years ago when my marriage fell apart. Too many bad memories, and to be truthful I hate the place with a\u00a0 passion. lol I can totally relate on the good cry!! I've had quite a few of those over the years, and yes - a\u00a0couple that nearly cost me my relationship with Doug over our wedding plans! So don't ever underestimate the power of a good cry but don't let others force you into one that isn't a \"good\" one!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>You're leaving for Jamaica from Toronto, driving from Ottawa next week and next weekend we're going to Ottawa!\u00a0We have 2 granddaughters there so with so much going on we have one that we still have to do Christmas with, hopefully next weekend, weather permitting! This time of the year it's so unpredictable with snow storms along the lake!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>You're absolutely right about the difference between getting married and having a wedding. And you do get caught up in it. You're on a \"happy\" cloud. I think we got into the same trap as you. When we decided to get married (we didn't have an \"engagement\" really, for specific reasons) and told everyone that we were doing it in Jamaica, it was the same reaction - \"Oh we're going\" and \"It's a good chance for a family vacation\" etc etc. Yeah and we know how that worked out. We didn't want kids at our wedding and that complicated things. Our kids are grown and our grandkids were all babies then so we knew our kids wouldn't have a proper vacation dealing with small children, or I wouldn't\u00a0so Doug put his foot down and said no kids. Then as people dropped out, the others were worried about paying more for the trip so they dropped out. In the end we had the last laugh because we ended up booking last minute and saved $300 each!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>It was the wedding coordinator in Jamaica that helped me get ready and both of them were our witnesses so our marriage license is signed by complete strangers! But hey - it is what it is and the end result was accomplished, and even now more than 4 years later I still sometimes have to remind myself of that!\u00a0 Secrets Wild Orchid - nice!!! I've heard so many good reviews of that resort! Are getting married out on the little pier??? It's so pretty!!! I would have loved to go back to Jamaica last October when we did our renewal but we both adore Mexico and hadn't been for several years so it just seemed the obvious choice to go to. We loved it but t's still on the agenda to get back to Jamaica. That was where we were supposed to go for our first anniversary but it was spent in the hospital instead so it's still on the list of \"want to do's\".<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm sorry to hear about your husband. That's a difficult diagnosis to deal with for sure!!! Yes - life really is too short. We found that out the hard way. By rights I shouldn't be here and thanks to Doug, I am. He's the one that pushed going to the hospital and it's a good thing he did. I used to know someone that was a paid firefighter and I remember he had all kinds of health issues too, and obviously the danger level would bother you!! I can understand that completely! Again, you deal with each day as it comes. Whatever is meant to be is going to be. All you can do is live and love together and hope for the best!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I had tons of stuff left over too!!!! Omg - that's so funny. I'm a law clerk so it becomes second nature to be organized and always planning so I did the same thing and got everything when everyone said they were going. You made me laugh on the advil, Tylenol and emergen-c. I think we took a year to use stuff up!!! And yes - small groups are of no interest to the resorts so any info is beneficial!! It was difficult in the beginning to see all the \"20 somethngs\" as you called them having their big weddings but I had to stop and think I did that too when I was a 20 something. Doug and I didn't want any fuss, and that's exactly what we got.\u00a0That's why we\u00a0ended up having\u00a0our renewal off site at a restaurant. I tried working with Azul Fives originally and they all want to stick you in an a la carte restaurant with everyone else and that was a no go for me. In the end what we had was perfect! We were 10 for dinner thanks to our planner and her assistant, \u00a0husband and daughter plus our photographer and his gf so it worked out fine.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Super bowl!! That's so cool you get to celebrate it on the beach!!! Who are your teams???? Doug is a Steelers fan and I'm a PATS fan so I've got a lot riding on this weekend!!! Another thing that is so similar! Freaky!! lol We went to a pre-season Steelers-Bills game in August since we live so close to the border so Doug got to see his team in action. He also got me tickets to a PATS Bills game a few Christmases ago, on Boxing Day no less. It was about -30 and we froze our butts off!! lol But it was\u00a0SOOOOOOO awesome!! I loved it!!\u00a0We're still trying to organize a Steelers\/PATS game which will happen one of these days!! Doug took me to Gillette Stadium on our way back from his parents for Xmas a year ago so I went camera crazy, plus we did the museum. I got Xmas money and spent it on Brady stuff and stickers for my truck. lol Yes - we're football geeks!!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We're off wine tasting this weekend and it's time to leave the office so I better finish this up and get out of here. Let me know how things are going before you leave if you have time. If not, have a wonderful wedding week and a magical wedding day!! I'm looking forward to seeing the photos!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>All the best. Have a good weekend!<\/p>\n<p>Ann<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n","PostKey":"a4ae99ea030a4643d239201096c6909c","CanDelete":true,"Attachments":[]},{"Id":22133,"Author":{"Id":284050,"Name":"2ndTimeMrs","Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"IsOnline":true},"Date":1453720970,"Content":"<p>Good morning Ann - Hope you had a great weekend. I saw your message Friday after work but after a few days of feeling sorry for myself last week I was behind the eight ball for last minute wedding prep so needed to get caught up. After scrambling for the last couple of days I figured I'd come back to work for a break <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\u00a0I finished my bouquet, Peter's\u00a0boutonniere and my Grandmother's corsage late last night so once I get home tonight I will post pictures on here.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Ok it's really starting to get scary how similar we are. I am originally from Toronto too (Mississauga to be exact) I've lived in Ottawa since 1998 but like you I hate\u00a0the city. It's so funny\u00a0because everyone always says how cold and unfriendly Toronto is but I don't find that at all. I have travelling coast to coast several times and can honestly say Ottawa is the most unfriendly city I've been to in Canada.\u00a0When my marriage fell apart I was actually going to pick up and move to Bermuda as I had several clients there at the time\u00a0but by the time I\u00a0sold my house and got my ducks in a row Peter came along and well the rest is history.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We're also wine lovers too. Have you and Doug ever been to Prince Edward County near Picton? If you haven't I highly recommend it for a weekend getaway. It's like Niagara where there are tons of wineries. Before we bought our boat a few years ago we used to spend most of our weekends in the summer months there touring all the wineries and adding to our collection -some weekends we were luck if any bottles made it home full <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/laugh.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':lol:' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Sorry about your PATS this past weekend. We're both Cheeseheads so we had our hearts broken when Green Bay got defeated the weekend before last by Arizona.\u00a0We're excited to watch Super Bowl 50\u00a0 on then beach though. I even had a Packers \"wedding\" Jersey made with the number 2 (for our wedding date) and my new last name (Hallinan).\u00a0\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I found it really hard too when everyone we invited started dropping out and the younger girls on here were posting their reviews saying things like \"we only had 30 people....etc\" Part of me would love to have a large group and be able to do a lot of the great ideas I've seen other brides do on here but like you said I did that already when I was in my 20's. I had a big wedding last time and look how that turned out. The wedding is only one day...the marriage is forever. We didn't want a big fuss either so in the end we got what we wanted.(I could have done without all the stress in between though)<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Originally I was against doing a AHR simply because I felt very bitter about everyone cancelling with obvious made up excuses or not even acknowledging the wedding invitation at all but now that we are getting closer to our wedding day everyone keeps saying when we come home they want to take us out to dinner. In an effort to avoid becoming 500lbs for all the meals out we decided we are\u00a0going to pick our favorite restaurant in Ottawa and tell everyone where and when we are going. Those who want to come with come and those who don't\u00a0oh well. We also don't want our wedding drawn out over months of people taking us out to congratulate us so we are going to make it clear to everyone what our wishes are and we are holding firm on them.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I hear ya about the resort not caring. Ever since I reduced my package (AKA how much $$ I'm bringing into the resort) The service level has gone way down. Secrets doesn't have reservations for dinner in their a la cartes but I know from having been there before that the French restaurant does require reservations if you want to sit inside. It is the nicest restaurant and I figured since we were just 6 people (before our witnesses had to cancel) this would be a nice compromise for our wedding reception. I contacted the restaurant booking team to see about reserving a table and they said the resort does not allow people to do that. I have to fight back and forth with them several times saying I was a past customer and I know they take reservations blah, blah, blah.... but they still wouldn't do it. It took me sending them a trip advisor review I found from another bride where she talks about booking a reservation at the restaurant for her FH and parents to have a pre-wedding dinner. Suddenly they were very accommodating. Same goes for the photographer. All the Secrets wedding packages have their photographer for 1 hour. We didn't know we were getting married that last time we were in Jamaica but we wanted nice pictures together so we hired their photographer to take our photos and quite frankly\u00a0I've seen better photos taken at the Sears Portrait Studio. That's why we hired Misha Earle. The resort\u00a0was still insisting their photographer has to also take pictures at\u00a0our wedding and I had to be firm with them. They tried to push me but then I reminded them that\u00a0I had to pay them $380 for the\u00a0\"privilege\" to bring in an outside vendor and that if their photographer attends my wedding and hinders our photographer's work then I will not be paying the vendor fee. Suddenly they backed off <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/wink.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=';)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Well I guess I should get back to work!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>-Nancy<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<blockquote  class=\"ipsBlockquote\" data-author=\"acw271011\" data-time=\"1453500397\">\n<div>\n<p>Hi Nancy,<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>It's nice to e-meet you!!\u00a0 Oh my goodness - your message gave me chills!!\u00a0 It's totally unbelievable how many similarities there are between us!!! It's a bit freaky!! lol\u00a0 First of all, I'm Toronto born but I spent about half of my life or a bit more in Ottawa, then came back to Toronto about 17 years ago when my marriage fell apart. Too many bad memories, and to be truthful I hate the place with a\u00a0 passion. lol I can totally relate on the good cry!! I've had quite a few of those over the years, and yes - a\u00a0couple that nearly cost me my relationship with Doug over our wedding plans! So don't ever underestimate the power of a good cry but don't let others force you into one that isn't a \"good\" one!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>You're leaving for Jamaica from Toronto, driving from Ottawa next week and next weekend we're going to Ottawa!\u00a0We have 2 granddaughters there so with so much going on we have one that we still have to do Christmas with, hopefully next weekend, weather permitting! This time of the year it's so unpredictable with snow storms along the lake!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>You're absolutely right about the difference between getting married and having a wedding. And you do get caught up in it. You're on a \"happy\" cloud. I think we got into the same trap as you. When we decided to get married (we didn't have an \"engagement\" really, for specific reasons) and told everyone that we were doing it in Jamaica, it was the same reaction - \"Oh we're going\" and \"It's a good chance for a family vacation\" etc etc. Yeah and we know how that worked out. We didn't want kids at our wedding and that complicated things. Our kids are grown and our grandkids were all babies then so we knew our kids wouldn't have a proper vacation dealing with small children, or I wouldn't\u00a0so Doug put his foot down and said no kids. Then as people dropped out, the others were worried about paying more for the trip so they dropped out. In the end we had the last laugh because we ended up booking last minute and saved $300 each!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>It was the wedding coordinator in Jamaica that helped me get ready and both of them were our witnesses so our marriage license is signed by complete strangers! But hey - it is what it is and the end result was accomplished, and even now more than 4 years later I still sometimes have to remind myself of that!\u00a0 Secrets Wild Orchid - nice!!! I've heard so many good reviews of that resort! Are getting married out on the little pier??? It's so pretty!!! I would have loved to go back to Jamaica last October when we did our renewal but we both adore Mexico and hadn't been for several years so it just seemed the obvious choice to go to. We loved it but t's still on the agenda to get back to Jamaica. That was where we were supposed to go for our first anniversary but it was spent in the hospital instead so it's still on the list of \"want to do's\".<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm sorry to hear about your husband. That's a difficult diagnosis to deal with for sure!!! Yes - life really is too short. We found that out the hard way. By rights I shouldn't be here and thanks to Doug, I am. He's the one that pushed going to the hospital and it's a good thing he did. I used to know someone that was a paid firefighter and I remember he had all kinds of health issues too, and obviously the danger level would bother you!! I can understand that completely! Again, you deal with each day as it comes. Whatever is meant to be is going to be. All you can do is live and love together and hope for the best!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I had tons of stuff left over too!!!! Omg - that's so funny. I'm a law clerk so it becomes second nature to be organized and always planning so I did the same thing and got everything when everyone said they were going. You made me laugh on the advil, Tylenol and emergen-c. I think we took a year to use stuff up!!! And yes - small groups are of no interest to the resorts so any info is beneficial!! It was difficult in the beginning to see all the \"20 somethngs\" as you called them having their big weddings but I had to stop and think I did that too when I was a 20 something. Doug and I didn't want any fuss, and that's exactly what we got.\u00a0That's why we\u00a0ended up having\u00a0our renewal off site at a restaurant. I tried working with Azul Fives originally and they all want to stick you in an a la carte restaurant with everyone else and that was a no go for me. In the end what we had was perfect! We were 10 for dinner thanks to our planner and her assistant, \u00a0husband and daughter plus our photographer and his gf so it worked out fine.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Super bowl!! That's so cool you get to celebrate it on the beach!!! Who are your teams???? Doug is a Steelers fan and I'm a PATS fan so I've got a lot riding on this weekend!!! Another thing that is so similar! Freaky!! lol We went to a pre-season Steelers-Bills game in August since we live so close to the border so Doug got to see his team in action. He also got me tickets to a PATS Bills game a few Christmases ago, on Boxing Day no less. It was about -30 and we froze our butts off!! lol But it was\u00a0SOOOOOOO awesome!! I loved it!!\u00a0We're still trying to organize a Steelers\/PATS game which will happen one of these days!! Doug took me to Gillette Stadium on our way back from his parents for Xmas a year ago so I went camera crazy, plus we did the museum. I got Xmas money and spent it on Brady stuff and stickers for my truck. lol Yes - we're football geeks!!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We're off wine tasting this weekend and it's time to leave the office so I better finish this up and get out of here. Let me know how things are going before you leave if you have time. If not, have a wonderful wedding week and a magical wedding day!! I'm looking forward to seeing the photos!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>All the best. Have a good weekend!<\/p>\n<p>Ann<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/blockquote>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n","PostKey":"d4add8c5d2ef0e0b707bd46e98b2c4f1","CanDelete":false,"Attachments":[]},{"Id":22147,"Author":{"Id":232000,"Name":"acw271011","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232000.jpg?_r=1434318164","PhotoWidth":570,"PhotoHeight":541,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":true},"Date":1453741450,"Content":"<p>Well now you really are starting to freak me out! lol Some of this is just uncanny!! I swear - it's just weird! I looked at a job in Bermuda too!! But Doug and I talked about it about 2 years ago, so a bit more recent than you and we just didn't feel the time was right! But geez.... talk about creepy! lol Yes - we did have a good weekend, as I hope you did! You're allowed to feel sorry for yourself, but given how close your wedding is, now is the time to be happy!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Before I forget, I have heard nothing but GREAT things about Misha Earle and the work of hers that I've seen is beautiful!! So unless things have really gone downhill since Doug and I got married in 2011, you will love her! We didn't have the budget for her back then, and I don't think she was available anyway. We used Merrick Cousley and he was wonderful! He was \"just starting out\" back then and to look at his photos now, he really has come a long way but I'm happy with what we have and it worked for us budget wise back then. I went higher last fall for our renewal but only because I knew what I wanted. It all turned out just fine in the end, which really I guess is all that matters.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Yeah - my PATS totally tanked yesterday. I don't get it! They were absolutely NOT the same team that played last weekend. That team just didn't show up in Denver. No clue where they were. But it's the biggest insult there is - to lose to the ponies just makes me sick and to lose to manning is even worse!!! The media will just go crazy over it and play up manning as if he's the second coming! And of course there are all the comments about the fact that PATS can't win when they don't cheat! grrrrr\u00a0 You want smack - I'll give you smack! lol The only good thing is that Panthers will make total mincemeat of manning - he's so washed up - so I will get satisfaction from watching that. Then manning can just fade away into the sunset like he should have done before now! Oh no - cheeseheads??? Really???? lmao\u00a0 You have my condolences...\u00a0 jk We have friends in Wisconsin. I know I don't need to say any more than that.... I was hoping Arizona would win yesterday - newton is too arrogant for my taste - but I knew Arizona would have zero chance against denver so it's ok that carolina won, if only for the reason of beating manning's ass!!! Ok - nuff said lol<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>It's just too freaky you asked me about Prince Edward County! lol My step daughter lives there!! Well in Belleville specifically. So yes - we've done a couple of the wineries out that way just on the way home from seeing our granddaughters. I can't think of the names off the top of my head - Sandbanks is one I think. We talk about going back that way again to check out a few more but Niagara is our favourite so we always end up\u00a0there, and it's so much closer for us (just an hour away). The icewine festival was great this year - we loved the food pairings that we chose, a couple of which were unusual but were delicious!! I'm a sucker for the sweeter wines so icewine is right at the top of my list. I think we added 8 more bottles this weekend\u00a0to the collection. Doug is griping now about when we're going to drink them!!! We had a sample of icewine last year that was\u00a0a 1999 so it was more like butterscotch\/caramel than icewine but it was soooooo good!! We ended up buying a bottle. They told us not to keep it more than about another year because it was already 15 years old and we still haven't opened it yet!! It's just such a heartbreak to know that once we drink it, it's gone!! lol I'm generally into Reislings and have just recently started with Pinot Grigio. Doug is a Guvertz (sp) drinker. Sorry - I know I can't spell that. We absolutely need to try to meet up sometime for wine tasting!!!!! That would be so cool!!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>You're doing your own flowers??? Wow - go you!! I couldn't have done anything like that if my life depended on it!! I am so without the creativity gene - it's awful!! I so envy anyone that can do the creative stuff because I definitely can't. I had one of the brides here even do my menu cards for me because I'm useless at that stuff. She did such a beautiful job! All I had to do was print them. She put together the file and sent it then I just arranged for the printing. She also did door hangers for me. I managed to do little tags for our maracas and little pouches for key and money holders but I had too many since we only used 4 but at least I made the attempt! lol They turned out ok. I wanted to do the passport invites or at least the boarding pass invites\u00a0but since everyone backed out there was no point. What kind of dress are you wearing???\u00a0 Shoes?? Hairpiece or veil??? You need to post this stuff!!! lol It's too bad you haven't done a full thread. The girls love to read them!! But you absolutely have to do a review thread with pics. Everyone would love to see it!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I hear you on the resorts. They make so much money from weddings but they still nickel and dime you any way they can, and if you have a small group then it's like your business just doesn't count. We had to pay $435 for the outside vendor fee in October\u00a0and we nearly got screwed over on that as well! They very nearly weren't gong to let the photographer in because the coordinator didn't notify them in advance, so we ended up paying over $2000 to have a photographer, and that was only for 5 hours. It's mind boggling how the costs can add up. I read some of what the girls go through and I just feel so badly for them. What day do you finish work? Are you staying at the airport?<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Another freaky thing - we live in Mississauga!! lol I hate it to be honest. Doug and I lived in Brampton when we first met and for a while afterwards, then moved to Burlington. I loved it but Doug commutes to Yonge & Sheppard so for him from Burlington was grueling. We finally had to look for something closer and looked in Newmarket but couldn't find something we really liked and it was under protest for me. I'm in downtown TO. We looked in Oakville but Doug picked apart every place we looked at. In the end it was Mississauga but my condition was west Mississauga only. I refuse to go into east Mississauga. You'd have to kill me first. So we're actually right on the border of Mississauga and Milton, which I tolerate only. Doug has just gone down to working from home 3 days a week so I've already broached the subject of going back to Burlington, since he would only have to go to the office 2 days a week. It's under consideration right now. He's worried that they'll cancel the program, he'll have to go back to\u00a05 days in the office\u00a0and that would mean moving again for him to be closer so we've decided to tough it out for one more year and see what happens. If the program continues then next year I want to go back towards Burlington or west Oakville, or even Stoney Creek. We're on the retirement countdown now and I'm hoping that it's only about 4 to 5 years away. That's the plan but if we keep taking hits in the stock market it could be longer. We have a camping trailer and Doug wants to take a year when we first retire to take the trailer on the road and just travel to all of the places that we've talked about over the years. There are so many places I would like to go. But the idea is that we'll settle everything, take off for a year then head south for good. I have arthritis in my back and every year gets harder and harder with the cold so going somewhere warm can't come quickly enough for me!!! lol<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Here's something for you to think about. We've started a group on facebook of brides from the site here. We're trying to plan a trip together as a group, with spouses. Because so many of them have just had their wedding, naturally finances are a\u00a0bit tight so we're thinking of trying to plan it for January next year (2017). Do it just like a wedding group - get a travel agent and try and get a good rate. We have western brides too so Vancouver and Calgary are also involved. If you think it's something you might be interested in let me know, and I can add you to the group if you like. It's difficult to put anything on this site for it just because it's completely public, whereas the FB group is private and closed. I think if we can really make it happen, it's going to be great. We already have a Toronto brides group that meets every couple of months, which is so much fun! We talk weddings all night, eat and drink and just have a blast looking at pictures and videos of the newly wed ones and encourage the ones who's weddings are still coming up. It's great. Being a coordinator on this site I've seen SO many brides come and go. There are a couple I still keep in touch with, and it's sort of cool to see them starting their families. I also do a bit of work with one of the vendors here - Joyce from Dream Weddings. That's a story for another day! lol Anyway, let me know what you think about the group trip.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I think you have every right to determine what you want to do for an \"AHR\", in whatever form it takes and stick to your guns. If people are upset, too bad. We lost friends over our wedding stuff, and as much as it made me sad, if we lost them over stuff like that, then they weren't really good friends to begin with!! If you want a restaurant for dinner one evening, the ones that really want to be there will be. The rest.... well screw 'em! lol I'm too old for crap like that now and life is just too short. We have enough to deal with with our kids so I am just not into it from outside people. Not worth it!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Ok. It's that time. I've done this in bits and pieces in between trying to get some work done and it's\u00a0time to pack up and get my train\u00a0thank goodness. At least the days are getting longer...<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Let me know how things come together before you leave if you have a minute!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Cheers!<\/p>\n<p>Ann<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n","PostKey":"a3473056ed78c1c4acb8621894c374c5","CanDelete":true,"Attachments":[]}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":6,"TotalPages":1,"CurrentPage":0,"NextPage":-1,"PreviousPage":-1,"LastPage":0},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
